+
+### Phase 22: WAI-ARIA Accessibility & Landmark Tree Extractor, RFC 7578 Multipart Upload / Verified Chunked Downloader & Executive Brief / Atomic Claim Cards Exporter
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/dom-aria-a11y-tree-extractor.cjs`**:
+  - `extractAriaAccessibilityTree({ html, visibleText })` and `findInteractiveTargetsByAriaRoleAndName(tree, { role, nameQuery, includeDisabled })`: extracts a structured WAI-ARIA landmark (`main`, `navigation`, `banner`, `contentinfo`, `form`, `dialog`, `alert`), interactive control (`button`, `link`, `textbox`, `searchbox`, `checkbox`, `radio`, `combobox`, `file_input`), and live region (`aria-live`, `role="alert"`) tree with resolved `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby` / `aria-describedby` names, exact UTF-16 `[startUtf16..endUtf16]` offsets, and deterministic selectors/bounds.
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/multipart-upload-and-chunk-downloader.cjs`**:
+  - `buildSafeMultipartFormDataPayload({ workspaceRoot, fields, fileAttachments, boundary })`: validates every attached file through `verifyFileSelectionPolicy` (`policy.cjs`), blocks forbidden `.env` / `.exe` / outside-workspace paths (`BROWSER_FORBIDDEN_ATTACHMENT`), computes SHA-256 digests, and produces an RFC 7578 `multipart/form-data` payload.
+  - `executeVerifiedChunkedDownload({ workspaceRoot, fileName, subDir, chunks, expectedSha256, maxBytes, signal })`: streams chunks into a `.part` staging file inside the allowed workspace folder via `resolveAllowedDownloadTarget`, respects `AbortSignal` and `maxBytes`, verifies SHA-256 integrity, and atomically finalizes the file.
+- **`desktop/windows/browser/executive-brief-and-claim-cards-exporter.cjs`**:
+  - `buildExecutiveBriefAndClaimCards(report)` and `saveExecutiveBriefAndClaimCardsViaWorkspace({ workspaceRoot, slug, report })`: generates an Executive Brief (`reports/<slug>-executive-brief.md`) and a machine-verifiable Atomic Claim Cards deck (`reports/<slug>-claim-cards.json`) with `claimCardId` SHA-256 digests, verbatim UTF-16 `[startUtf16..endUtf16]` quotes, distinct `pageDate` / `eventDate` / `fetchedAt`, and explicit bare-link rejections (`BARE_LINK_NOT_PROOF_OF_CLAIM`).
+- **Exposed via `shell.cjs` (`browser.extract_aria_tree`, `browser.build_multipart_form_payload`, `browser.execute_chunked_download`, `browser.export_executive_brief`) and verified in Subtests 36 and 37 (`47/47` total suites passing).**
